1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,941
Locker seventeen was empty. Lucia
checked the key again, Their contact had

2
00:00:04,941 --> 00:00:07,000
rented them the wrong mountain.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:11,667
The map showed two lodges with identical
lockers. One closed in summer;

4
00:00:11,667 --> 00:00:14,000
the other only opened in winter.

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:20,067
Their contact had left no address, just
a pine-stamped brass token with a

6
00:00:20,067 --> 00:00:21,000
horizontal scratch.

7
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:25,667
Jason called it damage. Lucia turned the
token over. The scratch crossed

8
00:00:25,667 --> 00:00:28,000
the tree at the old snowline.

9
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:32,941
The winter lodge stood below that line.
They followed the covered walkway

10
00:00:32,941 --> 00:00:35,000
instead of climbing another mile.

11
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:39,550
Locker seventeen there had a coin slot.
The brass token released it, and

12
00:00:39,550 --> 00:00:42,000
their pouch fell into Jason's waiting
hands.

13
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:46,789
Inside were their fee and the original
key deposit. Their contact had paid

14
00:00:46,789 --> 00:00:49,000
for directions nobody bothered to read.

15
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:55,125
Jason kept the money. Lucia kept the
map, She would charge him for the

16
00:00:55,125 --> 00:00:56,000
scenic route.
